  "implementation": {
    "engine": "AuxiliaryChannelFiltering replaces the channel preparation8MP guard and dense input/output loops with sparse/file-backed stored-sample mapping. Existing dense or paged basic raster kernels execute unchanged.",
    "numeric": "Raw stored coverage/auxiliary spot density is filtered independently of display indication/Solidity. Float numeric proxies are tagged linear without transfer conversion. Final values use the old opaque grayscale/quantization policy across all stored samples, including unselected values. Source color, other channels, identity/name/options/spot/source-gray metadata and selection remain unchanged.",
    "native_API": "Existing native Filter dialogs now admit the eight basic kinds on large alpha/spot/QuickMask targets, including hidden QuickMask and standalone selection documents. Existing channel.edit action=filter and filter.repeat share preparation/history. channels.filtering describes actual supported kinds, capacity and legacy-only exception.",
    "legacy_Liquify": "Audit found existing direct channel API accepted bounded Liquify while native channels excluded it. Preserve that path and cap, tested against the archived dense preparation and unchanged kernel; no new native workspace claim.",
    "versions": "No new command, format, model, tool, modifier or global shortcut. Native89/Actions58/265typed commands unchanged. Semantic channel-filter Actions and Adobe descriptor/runtime support remain explicitly unsupported."
  },
